# `for (;;) { try { s += ..; if (..) break; } catch { hits++; } } boom(s);`: the text is taken out of its builder on the edge that leaves the loop, under the handler of the block that is left. What stands behind the loop does not stand under that handler.
# f1 = boom, f2 = build
